      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_debug_print_read_bounded_by_declared_length",
      "fine_trace_step": 12,
      "description": "Root cause. In the staged vulnerable source `CDF_DEBUG` makes `DPRINTF` a live `printf` call, but this format uses `%s` instead of a precision-bounded specifier, so the declared property length `l` is ignored and the print treats `inp[i].pi_str.s_buf` as an unbounded C string. The fix changes this to `%.*s` and passes `(int)l` as the bound."
    },
